From: TheWeaklessOne <41053514+TheWeaklessOne@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: change a command mode DSI refresh rate without a modeset

A command mode DSI panel scans out at its own frame length and paces the
host with TE; the host never transmits vertical porches. A mode that only
stretches the vertical front porch at the same pixel clock (how gamescope
generates its 40-120 Hz modes) needs no link or DPU reconfiguration, but
DRM sees a new mode and does a full modeset: the panel is disabled,
unprepared, powered up and initialised again, and the screen blinks.

Add two optional drm_panel hooks, can_switch_mode() and switch_mode(), and
drm_panel_bridge_get_panel() to reach the panel behind the msm DSI bridge.

The DPU CRTC skips the modeset (clears mode_changed in its atomic check)
only when all of these hold, and does a full modeset otherwise:
- the msm.dpu_seamless_vfp parameter is on (default; writable at runtime);
- the CRTC is active before and after, on the same single encoder;
- the encoder drives a command mode panel on one non-bonded DSI interface;
- old and new adjusted modes differ in the vertical front porch only (same
  clock, horizontal timings, vdisplay, vsync length, flags);
- the panel's can_switch_mode() accepts the transition;
- nothing else already requires a modeset (CTM toggle, CDM, clone mode,
  active or connector changes).

The commit then, from the CRTC's atomic_begin and after the previous frame
reached the panel, updates the encoder's cached mode, reprograms the tear
check for the new vtotal (the sync counter height also covers the old
frame length, for the frame the panel may still run at it), updates the
DSI host's mode in place and calls the panel's switch_mode(). DRM updates
crtc->mode and the vblank timestamping constants on every commit, and the
DPU bandwidth vote follows the new adjusted mode through the CRTC check.

drm_panel_funcs grows two members at its end. Only the msm DSI path calls
them, on the panel behind the DSI host, so panel modules built against the
old header stay usable elsewhere but must not sit behind msm DSI.

Rebased onto Linux 7.4 (port v1.5 kernel-sm8550-74): the panel bridge moved
from drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/panel.c into drivers/gpu/drm/drm_panel.c and its
declarations from drm_bridge.h into drm_panel.h; the panel bridge is now the
drm_panel itself (drm_bridge_to_panel()), so drm_panel_bridge_get_panel()
returns that.
